<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Goldfields mine workers to march Dec 31.</title>
<headline>Goldfields mine workers to march Dec 31.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>About 7,000 workers at a Goldfields of South Africa Ltd  mine plan to march on Tuesday to protest against the mine's insistence that they work on New Year's Day to make up for lost production, a union said.</p>
<p>The National Union of Mineworkers said on Monday workers at Libanon gold mine near Johannesburg asked for a day off on December 24 to do Christmas shopping but could not agree with management on the date to make up for the lost day. The march will start at 1300 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;(Workers) were prepared to make up for the lost production day on Saturday, January 4, but management insists that workers should work on January 1,&quot; the union said in a statement.</p>
<p>The mine could not be reached for comment.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
